<section class="section has-text-centered">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="has-text-weight-bold is-size-1 is-size-3-mobile is-uppercase">Progressive Boat</p>
    <p class="projectdescription is-size-5">
    In a sea of mundane boat conventions drowning in sales pitches, Progressive set sail on an irreverent journey to disrupt the status quo. Acting as both designer and creative, I helped shape the vision from the start with the Captain and his Mate — insurance-themed shanty singers who roamed boat shows crooning about coverage and dropping dad jokes sharp enough to make even a shipwrecked sailor grin.
<br><br>
We pushed the irreverence further with experiences like an augmented reality singing waverunner disguised as a bass, supersized claw machines, and a live fortune-telling booth from the Ferry Cod-mother. Alongside these activations, I led the creation of a new sub-brand for how Progressive shows up in boating, ensuring the work felt consistent, authentic, and ownable across every touchpoint.
<br><br>
 The result was more than entertainment. Progressive transformed dull boat conventions into a raucous playground of laughter and unforgettable experiences, carving out a place in boating culture that no competitor could touch.
    <p class="has-text-weight-bold is-size-4">Collaborators:</p>
    <p class="collabnames is-family-secondary has-text-weight-bold is-size-4 is-italic">Gary Baker // Jimmy Tanner // Sebastien Theroux <br> Julia Colasanti // Sal Delaquilla // Chris Blechar</p>
  </div>
</section>

